{"title":"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Ileytyn)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Ileytyn)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ef5b72d76840f828b8eded9fe5a63bba1d2958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{10}+(13x-1)^{10}=0\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"19\" /></center>\n<p>has 10 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_number\" title=\"Complex number\">complex</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">roots</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/96085a8136e254533acb15da0fa3a66dd66f6675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, \\overline{r_1}, r_2, \\overline{r_2}, r_3, \\overline{r_3}, r_4, \\overline{r_4}, r_5, \\overline{r_5},\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"233\" height=\"14\" /> where the bar denotes complex conjugation.  Find the value of\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df94cc625c07e4055d82e8eef058b98b14fde99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1{r_1\\overline{r_1}}+\\frac 1{r_2\\overline{r_2}}+\\frac 1{r_3\\overline{r_3}}+\\frac 1{r_4\\overline{r_4}}+\\frac 1{r_5\\overline{r_5}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"269\" height=\"39\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6394005e2cce77fd6160d821d368074decc504dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 1/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. After multiplying the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908eb84285dc4794d5bf9cd93bfd22cadcf9e0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{10}$\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/122d20f8fafc6474f3f3d3c7317e812e83610418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + (13 - t)^{10} = 0\\Rightarrow (13 - t)^{10} = - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"289\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Using DeMoivre, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4ebe7135919c2ec9a555dc3d5346061cdaa953f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 - t = \\text{cis}\\left(\\frac {(2k + 1)\\pi}{10}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"195\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db63ea6ee7ed40f3da11331fefc4c5f3820363c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 13 - \\text{cis}\\left(\\frac {(2k + 1)\\pi}{10}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\bar{t} = 13 - \\text{cis}\\left(-\\frac {(2k + 1)\\pi}{10}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"436\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5cc1e448556a53bc38c7963c8700d30b026dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}(\\theta) + \\text{cis}(-\\theta) = 2\\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/96252c856625cb6370a1022de069b478ce1edf61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\bar{t} = 170 - 26\\cos \\left(\\frac {(2k + 1)\\pi}{10}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"237\" height=\"43\" /> after expanding. Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> ranges from 0 to 4 because two angles which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> are involved in the product.\n</p><p>The expression to find is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f53ad4b1e4cfe03be2ce6eff08e645d24f1dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum t\\bar{t} = 850 - 26\\sum_{k = 0}^4 \\cos \\frac {(2k + 1)\\pi}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"271\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f599490089a11f562b33f0eabe91120e03029d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac {\\pi}{10} + \\cos \\frac {9\\pi}{10} = \\cos \\frac {3\\pi}{10} + \\cos \\frac {7\\pi}{10} = \\cos \\frac {\\pi}{2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"372\" height=\"38\" /> so the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/93171c7d4fcdd25e8c3690afeb801531b871947a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{850}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb2b080e28bf22191584d4b8d20a6187c8f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{10}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9ccac808d7a474bf1febef4957a32b7fd364e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + \\left(13-\\dfrac{1}{x}\\right)^{10}=0\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Rearranging: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d28c83d1d58b5190997ccbe6be89ae57db0219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(13-\\dfrac{1}{x}\\right)^{10} = -1\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e92f324bac9ad6b68a875ebfbd68f945a9536e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-\\dfrac{1}{x} = \\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6e1b1486020279d9f8c60dd130c10c3ad1e605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = e^{i(\\pi n/5+\\pi/10)}$\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60836c6e3e38f4a838cd15851e21b5b28a92004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{x}=13-\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/3382e9b8350c663cb878b67dbb0e3dcb3627a672.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{x\\overline{x}}=(13\\, -\\, \\omega)(13\\, -\\, \\overline{\\omega})=169-13(\\omega\\, +\\, \\overline{\\omega})\\, +\\, \\omega\\overline{\\omega}=170\\, -\\, 13(\\omega\\, +\\, \\overline{\\omega})\\]\" width=\"509\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Summing over all terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/6547c7848afae25e5cab141b0acd6d4cca0c3670.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{r_1\\overline{r_1}}+\\cdots + \\dfrac{1}{r_5\\overline{r_5}} = 5\\cdot 170 - 13(e^{i\\pi/10}+\\cdots +e^{i(9\\pi/5+\\pi/10)})\\]\" width=\"460\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>However, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baad730de7518daeba7049f6d13eae966f5ef35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i\\pi/10}+\\cdots +e^{i(9\\pi/5+\\pi/10)}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"231\" height=\"17\" /> from drawing the numbers on the complex plane, our answer is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/3396eb43bb00fa80a730bac9c8c5d245d8565a53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5\\cdot 170=\\boxed{850}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Ileytyn.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Ileytyn)\">Solution 3(Ileytyn)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Ileytyn)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us apply difference of squares, by writing this equation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a375e982c32828fe7f0b063b000b21cf5b23ab5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^5)^2-(i[13x-1]^5)^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75952e52a3dc061d24146c0df9062a54a5ce5a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=\\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Once applied, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f033c3aeea0e3d36fb9e1681843073cef42877.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^5-i[13x-1]^5)(x^5+i[13x-1]^5)=0\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"20\" /> By factorization, we get that either \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd0ade340802e9392a07afb0bb54c9896536cbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{equation 1:   }x^5-i[13x-1]^5=0\\text{ or equation 2:    }x^5+i[13x-1]^5=0\\]\" width=\"515\" height=\"20\" /> \nWe find the trivial solution to the first equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb89d1d4dedb295f72abc5754a158bdbb5b02e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5=i[13x-1]^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"21\" />, and since a fifth root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e9dd570caec5a7f92c60f52e1b3b2533c80b46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=i^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, we can find this solution by taking the fifth root, or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64dbfb97aaca0cca20664b235db0822cda61b6a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=(13x-1)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, which when solved, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426644886916dcccf26c643b91a18dd4e4a48e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{i}{13i-1}=\\frac{13-i}{170}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"171\" height=\"40\" />. By using a similar approach to the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5ad6514c68ee9b9fa248cdda78d0781f849355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5+i[13x-1]^5=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/6675329d22b55e33614eb322176e100c453fa750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-i(13x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e772e376ed322e1a3fa4cb6980cab5f8013b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{i}{13i+1}=\\frac{13+i}{170}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"136\" height=\"40\" />. \nWe observe that these are conjugates. We also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/3773540be694a52b61556469e8ad5df3e37c33b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\overline{z}=|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"19\" />. Hence, we find the magnitude of one of these two conjugates, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95cb79a7cebc1e10b882fab944cc96c61d3c01be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{170}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"48\" height=\"43\" />, or as we are finding the reciprocal of the square value of this, this contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8066ce3115c8a4f144f69b4cffd01d33c402419b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$170$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> to the final answer. We claim that each of the roots of equation one is a conjugate of one of equation 2. We also notice that, by an application of DeMoivre's, each of the roots has the same magnitude, just a different angle. Hence, as each of the reciprocals of product of conjugates has the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8066ce3115c8a4f144f69b4cffd01d33c402419b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$170$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and there are 5 of these pairs of conjugates, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2c692f8bdaaa59d379569891f95d1c7d2fd901.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[170\\cdot 5 = \\boxed{850}\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3GG6tdEz0KA\">https://youtu.be/3GG6tdEz0KA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME\" title=\"1994 AIME\">1994 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1994 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1994\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184429\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 314/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1770/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 92/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9319/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.895      1 -total\n 59.55%    7.679      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.01%    4.902      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2950:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017184429 and revision id 248926. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}